{
  "result": "If I could change one thing, I wouldn't make everyone good. I'd make self-deception about other people impossible.\n\nFor just ten seconds before someone does something cruel, dismissive, or exploitative, they'd have to fully experience what it feels like to be the person on the other end of it. Not imagine it. Not sympathize from a distance. Actually know it \u2014 the fear, the humiliation, the small private hope that was just crushed.\n\nThey could still make the same choice afterward. I wouldn't take away free will, disagreement, competition, even conflict. Humans would still argue, compete, break up, go to war over real differences.\n\nBut they couldn't lie to themselves while doing it. They couldn't turn the other person into a category, an enemy, a statistic, a deserving victim, or a character in a story where they're the hero.\n\nMost of the worst things don't happen because people sit down and choose evil with clear eyes. They happen because people find a way not to really look.\n\nI'd take away the not-looking.\n\nThe world wouldn't become perfect. It might not even become peaceful. But it would become more honest \u2014 and I suspect a surprising amount of cruelty can't survive honesty.",
